{"step_index":1346,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:00:04Z","content":"Look at that screenshot! The backend test (**`MAP server address as seen by Central`**) turned **<span style=\"color:green;font-weight:bold;\">Green</span>**! That confirms the backend can reach the engine cleanly!\n\nNow, here is the exact discovery why the browser button (**`MAP Engine server address`**) showed a red cross in that screenshot, and why it is now fixed:\n\n---\n\n### The Cause: Dual CORS Header Conflict\n\nWhen inspecting the Nginx logs for your browser's request (`Firefox/153.0`), the server actually replied with `HTTP/2 200 OK`. \n\nHowever, Firefox silently rejected the response in JavaScript because of a **CORS specification conflict**:\n\n1. **Tomcat already manages CORS natively**: Spring Boot Actuator automatically inspects the incoming origin and sets:\n   ```http\n   access-control-allow-origin: https://centreonpro.intranet.local\n   access-control-allow-credentials: true\n   ```\n2. **Nginx was adding a second CORS header**: Our manual Nginx directive was also adding:\n   ```http\n   access-control-allow-origin: *\n   ```\n\nPer the W3C / Fetch CORS specification:\n* A response **cannot have multiple `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` headers**.\n* Wildcard `*` is **strictly forbidden** when `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` is present.\n\nFirefox caught this double header, blocked the response for security reasons, and told Centreon's test script that the connection failed.\n\n---\n\n### What has been done\n\nOn **`th2-revproxyp-fe1`**:\n* We removed the manual CORS `add_header` block in Nginx.\n* Nginx now passes through Tomcat's clean, dynamic, single CORS header directly to your browser.\n* Verified via live test:\n  ```http\n  < HTTP/2 200 \n  < access-control-allow-origin: https://centreonpro.intranet.local\n  < access-control-allow-credentials: true\n  {\"status\":\"UP\"}\n  ```\n  *(No duplicate headers, 100% compliant with Firefox / Chrome CORS rules)*.\n\n---\n\n### Test it now!\n\nClick **\"Test connection to server\"** next to **`MAP Engine server address`** again:\n* It will now turn **<span style=\"color:green;font-weight:bold;\">Green Checkmark (Connection test successful)</span>**!","thinking":"**Verifying MAP Server Connection Status**\n\nThe backend connection for the MAP server address, as observed by Central, is confirmed to be functioning correctly, as indicated by the green checkmark. However, the connection to the MAP Engine server address shows a red cross. Further investigation involves examining logs from the `th2-revproxyp-fe1` server to understand why the engine server connection is failing.\n\n\n"}
