{"step_index":1355,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:11:06Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-10T19:11:06+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-10T19:11:06+04:00\n{\"File\":\"/home/koby/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md\",\"LineNumber\":3,\"LineContent\":\"## Server Onboarding to IaC \\u0026 Semaphore (Standard Operating Procedure)\"}\n{\"File\":\"/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/log/cli-20260908_102752.log\",\"LineNumber\":702,\"LineContent\":\"## Server Onboarding to IaC \\u0026 Semaphore (Standard Operating Procedure)\"}\n{\"File\":\"/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/log/cli-20260908_102752.log\",\"LineNumber\":762,\"LineContent\":\"ERROR: logging before google.Init: W0908 17:51:13.632209   17443 permission_grant_store.go:366] ignoring invalid allow entry \\\"command(cat \\u003c\\u003c 'EOF' \\u003e ~/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md\\\\n# Global Rules \\u0026 Memory — Antigravity\\\\n\\\\n## Server Onboarding to IaC \\u0026 Semaphore (Standard Operating Procedure)\\\\n\\\\nThis workflow is permanently recorded for onboarding any new or legacy server into `infra-management-system` and Semaphore.\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Zone \\u0026 Network Reality (Hard Rule)\\\\n* **Never mix network zones**: Inter-VLAN corporate firewalls strictly isolate DEV runners from PROD subnets.\\\\n* Hosts with PROD naming (`*p-*`) or on PROD subnets (e.g. `172.30.39.0/24`, `172.30.230-231.0/24`) **must** be placed in `inventories/prod/hosts.yml`.\\\\n* **Runner routing**:\\\\n  - `dev` -\\u003e `th2-ansid-run1` (DEV VLANs `172.30.242-243.0/24`)\\\\n  - `PROD` -\\u003e `th2-ansip-run1` (`172.30.199.225`, routes to datacenter \\u0026 Martinique PROD)\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Runner SSH Key \\u0026 Host Setup (`spui-runner`)\\\\n* **SSH Port**: `30`\\\\n* **Account**: `spui-runner`, group `SSH_Users` (in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` AllowGroups).\\\\n* **Sudoers**: `/etc/sudoers.d/spui-runner` with `spui-runner ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL`.\\\\n* **Authorized Keys** in `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner`:\\\\n  - **PROD**: `ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFW7ywu9PSVguYkbxDRMkU8FH/Ws09CDTWUSylusKkDA semaphore-runner-prod`\\\\n  - **DEV / VAL**: `ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFXxaA6I6XHKt1N9KMolZQQ7abBDA3r+RDl3iFc3l/Jo semaphore-runner`\\\\n* **Manual bootstrap script**: `playbooks/bootstrap-spui-runner-manual.sh \\u003czone\\u003e`.\\\\n* **Warning**: Never close the active root/superuser session before verifying `spui-runner` login due to `AllowGroups`.\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Inventory Declaration Pattern\\\\n* In `inventories/\\u003cenv\\u003e/hosts.yml`:\\\\n  ```yaml\\\\n  all:\\\\n    hosts:\\\\n      \\u003chostname\\u003e:\\\\n        ansible_host: \\u003cip\\u003e\\\\n        ansible_port: 30\\\\n        ansible_user: spui-runner\\\\n    children:\\\\n      \\u003cdedicated_group\\u003e:\\\\n        hosts:\\\\n          \\u003chostname\\u003e:\\\\n  ```\\\\n* **Isolation**: Keep new hosts OUT of shared application groups (`frontaux`, `backends`, `databases`) unless explicitly requested.\\\\n* **Validate locally**:\\\\n  ```bash\\\\n  ansible-inventory -i inventories/\\u003cenv\\u003e/hosts.yml --graph\\\\n  ansible-inventory -i inventories/\\u003cenv\\u003e/hosts.yml --host \\u003chostname\\u003e\\\\n  ```\\\\n\\\\n### 4. Git \\u0026 Automated Merge Request\\\\n* 1 subject = 1 branch = 1 MR.\\\\n* Automatically publish and create the MR in one shot via GitLab push options:\\\\n  ```bash\\\\n  git checkout -b feat/onboard-\\u003chostname\\u003e-\\u003cenv\\u003e\\\\n  git add inventories/\\u003cenv\\u003e/hosts.yml\\\\n  git commit -m \\\\\\\"feat(inventory): add \\u003chostname\\u003e to \\u003cenv\\u003e inventory\\\\\\\"\\\\n  git push -u -o merge_request.create -o merge_request.target=main -o merge_request.title=\\\\\\\"feat(inventory): add \\u003chostname\\u003e to \\u003cenv\\u003e inventory\\\\\\\" origin feat/onboard-\\u003chostname\\u003e-\\u003cenv\\u003e\\\\n  ```\\\\n\\\\n### 5. Semaphore Verification\\\\n* Once merged, Semaphore's 