\n22: * **Warning**: Never close the active root/superuser session before verifying `spui-runner` login due to `AllowGroups`.\n23: \n24: ### 3. Inventory Declaration Pattern\n25: * In `inventories/<env>/hosts.yml`:\n26:   ```yaml\n27:   all:\n28:     hosts:\n29:       <hostname>:\n30:         ansible_host: <ip>\n31:         ansible_port: 30\n32:         ansible_user: spui-runner\n33:     children:\n34:       <dedicated_group>:\n35:         hosts:\n36:           <hostname>:\n37:   ```\n38: * **Isolation**: Keep new hosts OUT of shared application groups (`frontaux`, `backends`, `databases`) unless explicitly requested.\n39: * **Validate locally**:\n40:   ```bash\n41:   ansible-inventory -i inventories/<env>/hosts.yml --graph\n42:   ansible-inventory -i inventories/<env>/hosts.yml --host <hostname>\n43:   ```\n44: \n45: ### 4. Git & Automated Merge Request\n46: * 1 subject = 1 branch = 1 MR.\n47: * Automatically publish and create the MR in one shot via GitLab push options:\n48:   ```bash\n49:   git checkout -b feat/onboard-<hostname>-<env>\n50:   git add inventories/<env>/hosts.yml\n51:   git commit -m \"feat(inventory): add <hostname> to <env> inventory\"\n52:   git push -u -o merge_request.create -o merge_request.target=main -o merge_request.title=\"feat(inventory): add <hostname> to <env> inventory\" origin feat/onboard-<hostname>-<env>\n53:   ```\n54: \n55: ### 5. Semaphore Verification\n56: * Once merged, Semaphore's inventory follows `main`.\n57: * Execute read-only fact gathering via `playbooks/check-distro-kernel.yml` with `--limit <hostname>`:\n58:   - PROD: Template ID `131` (*Check Linux Distro and Kernel - PROD (recon)*)\n59:   - DEV: Template ID `130` (*Check Linux Distro and Kernel - DEV*)\n60: * Verify status reports `ONLINE` with accurate OS and kernel details.\n61: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":1358,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:11:11Z","thinking":"**Documenting Configuration Details**\n\nInitial focus is on documenting the Centreon Map reverse proxy architecture and passwordless DNS-01 Let's Encrypt issuance through PowerDNS, specifically `th2-dnsp-mst1`. Next, documenting a Tomcat RFC 7230 duplicate `Host:` trap and a dual CORS conflict trap is needed. Finally, consider documenting internal network routing and proxy bypass for `outremer-telecom.fr`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Append Centreon Map & Reverse Proxy Architecture rules and memory","EndLine":61,"Instruction":"Add Section on Centreon Map & Reverse Proxy Architecture","ReplacementContent":"* Verify status reports `ONLINE` with accurate OS and kernel details.\n\n---\n\n## Centreon Map Architecture & Reverse Proxy Standard Operating Procedure\n\n### 1. Topology & IP Mapping\n* **Central Web / PHP Backend**: `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49:30`)\n* **Map Engine (Tomcat Spring Boot)**: `th2-centprop-map1` (`172.30.198.50:9443` HTTPS)\n* **Reverse Proxy**: `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:30` internal DMZ, `109.62.64.18` public VIP)\n* **PowerDNS Master**: `th2-dnsp-mst1` (`172.30.198.162:30`, user `superuser`, passwordless SSH + sudo `pdnsutil`)\n* **Public Domain**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`\n\n### 2. Passwordless DNS-01 Challenge Workflow\n* To generate or renew Let's Encrypt certificates for `*.outremer-telecom.fr`:\n  - Run certbot with manual DNS hooks ([`pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh) & [`pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh)).\n  - Hooks connect directly to `superuser@172.30.198.162:30` via `id_ed25519` key and execute `sudo pdnsutil replace-rrset` / `increase-serial`.\n  - No external APIs or credentials required.\n\n### 3. Nginx Reverse Proxy Rules (Port 9443 on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`)\n* **Vhost location**: `/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`\n* **Avoid the RFC 7230 Duplicate Host Trap**:\n  - In Nginx, multiple `proxy_set_header` directives with the same name in the same block do NOT overwrite each other; they send duplicate HTTP header fields.\n  - DO NOT include `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` inside `location /` if custom `proxy_set_header Host ...` is also defined.\n  - Sending duplicate `Host:` headers causes Apache Tomcat to immediately reject requests with `400 Bad Request`.\n* **CORS Handling**:\n  - Tomcat Spring Boot Actuator handles CORS natively and dynamically reflects the requesting origin (e.g. `https://centreonpro.intranet.local` or `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`) with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`.\n  - DO NOT inject manual `add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*'` in Nginx, as browsers strictly reject duplicate CORS origins and reject `*` when credentials are true.\n\n### 4. Workstation & Forward Proxy Environment (Debian Trixie)\n* Corporate forward proxy runs on Squid (`172.16.75.9:3128`).\n* Corporate firewall drops traffic from internal LAN (`10.x.x.x`) to public VIPs (no Hairpin NAT).\n* Internal workstations accessing `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` MUST:\n  1. Map `172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` in `/etc/hosts`.\n  2. Add `outremer-telecom.fr, .outremer-telecom.fr` to `no_proxy` / `NO_PROXY` in `/etc/environment` and GNOME `ignore-hosts` (`gsettings`).\n  3. This bypasses Squid for local domains while keeping `apt update` (Debian mirrors) 100% operational through the proxy.\n","StartLine":60,"TargetContent":"* Verify status reports `ONLINE` with accurate OS and kernel details.\n","TargetFile":"/home/koby/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md","toolAction":"Committing knowledge to AGENTS.md","toolSummary":"Update AGENTS.md memory"}}]}
