{"step_index":1365,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:11:31Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-10T19:11:31+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-10T19:11:31+04:00\nFile Path: `file:///home/koby/.ansible/.remember/remember.md`\nTotal Lines: 23\nTotal Bytes: 2459\nShowing lines 1 to 23\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Handoff\n2: \n3: ## State\n4: I tried deploying `~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub` (koby@debian-trixie) to `172.30.249.209` (root, port 22) via `playbooks/deploy-ssh-key.yml`. SSH auth + vault decrypt both worked, but the play fails at \"Gathering Facts\": `/usr/bin/python3` doesn't exist on that host. User explicitly said **do not install anything on 172.30.249.209**, so I stopped. No changes were made on the target; no `changed` tasks ran.\n5: \n6: ## Next\n7: 1. Diagnose the remote host with `-m raw` (no Python needed): `cat /etc/os-release; which python3 python; ls /usr/bin/python*` — I proposed this command but user stopped before running it.\n8: 2. If Python exists at a non-standard path: set `ansible_python_interpreter` in the vars file, no install needed.\n9: 3. If Python is genuinely absent: this blocks any non-raw Ansible module against this host — will need user's explicit OK before any install, or an install-free path (e.g. `raw` + manual `authorized_keys` append via shell heredoc).\n10: \n11: ## Context\n12: - `playbooks/deploy-ssh-key.yml` has an uncommitted local change: `become_method: sudo` → `become_method: ansible.builtin.sudo`. Left as-is, not committed.\n13: - `playbooks/group_vars/all/vault.yml` (DNS/certs secrets) auto-loads for ANY playbook targeting `all`, including unrelated ones like this SSH-key playbook — known gotcha, requires `--vault-password-file` even when the playbook itself uses no vault vars. Vault password: \"koby\".\n14: - Bash sandbox blocks outbound SSH to non-whitelisted hosts; user had to run the ansible-playbook command themselves via `!` prefix (auto-mode classifier blocks `dangerouslyDisableSandbox` for this even from me).\n15: - Ran into a separate local bug: `ansible-playbook` errors with \"requires blocking IO on stdin/stdout/stderr\" in this shell — worked around with `script -qec \"...\" /dev/null` to allocate a pty.\n16: - 172.30.249.209 has no inventory entry (ad hoc `-i \"172.30.249.209,\"` used); not documented anywhere else — its OS/purpose is unknown to me.\n17: \n18: ## Automated SSH & KeePass Integration\n19: - Tool: `/home/koby/.local/bin/kssh` (symlinked from `~/.ansible/scripts/kssh.py`).\n20: - Whenever user asks to SSH to a server, automatically run `kssh <server>` or query `~/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json` via `build_kdbx_pool.py`.\n21: - Auto-extracts IP, port (e.g. 30), user, key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`), and password.\n22: - Attempts passwordless key (`koby-bowser-ansible` or target user) first; falls back to `sshpass` using the database password.\n23: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
